# Cenote Scout's ruling: "If a resolving spell or ability instructs a specific creature to explore but that creature has left the
# battlefield, the creature still explores. If you reveal a nonland card this way, you won't put a +1/+1 counter on anything,
# but you may put the revealed card into your graveyard." (CR 701.44c.) With the Scout's trigger on the stack Bot1 Bolts its
# own Scout. The Scout dies first; the trigger then resolves: Mox Jet, a nonland card, is revealed from Bot1's library (the Scout's
# controller as it last was) and Bot1 puts it into the graveyard. The graveyard holds the Scout, the Bolt and Mox Jet.

